WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
How to use your Thrive Forward Guide.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.200
This guide was made for you. You can read it
alone, with a mentor, or in a group.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.440
Two topics we cover.
What is inside your guidebook?

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.000
How to use it to rebuild
confidence and find work.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.600
Discussion points. Your skills matter.
CV support.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.720
Interview practice. Wellbeing first.
Peer mentoring, and digital skills and safety.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:30.290
“My qualifications are from another country.
Can this still help me?”

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.330
“I don’t have perfect English.
Is this guide still for me?”

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:41.010
Yes, this guide is built around your journey.
It includes CV help for overseas qualifications,

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.650
multilingual phrases,
and support for every step.

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:50.210
“I have been out of work for a long time.
I don’t know how to explain the gap in my CV.”

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:56.130
Possible approaches. Section 3 of the guide
helps you frame employment gaps

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:59.000
honestly and confidently for UK employers.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.890
LaunchPad (coming soon) includes AI interview practice,
so you can build confidence before the real thing.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:09.810
Your peer mentor can help you
tell your professional story.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:13.500
Your journey is your strength, not a weakness.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.460
Quick facts. Available in Arabic, Somali,

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.100
Tigrinya, Yoruba and French. Free on any phone,
tablet, or printed copy.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:28.740
You are not starting from zero. You bring
wisdom, strength, and great potential.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.780
Thrive Forward walks with you every step of the way.
